* Simplified behavioural LM7805, written for circuit-tutor (not the vendor model).
* 5 V out with about 2 V dropout, 5 mA quiescent current, 0.05 ohm output resistance.
* The load current is drawn from IN (series pass element) and the GND pin carries only the
* quiescent current, so input current and dissipation (VIN - VOUT) * IOUT are right.
* Pin order matches the registry line: in gnd out
.subckt LM7805 in gnd out
breg n1 gnd v = min(5, max(v(in, gnd) - 2, 0))
rout n1 n2 0.05
vsense n2 out 0
fpass in gnd vsense 1
bq in gnd i = 5m * min(max(v(in, gnd), 0), 1)
.ends LM7805
